config BR2_PACKAGE_FCP_SUPPORT
	bool "fcp-support"
	depends on BR2_INIT_SYSTEMD
	depends on BR2_USE_MMU
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_LIB
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_LIB_HWDEP
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ALSA_LIB_MIXER
	select BR2_PACKAGE_JSON_C
	select BR2_PACKAGE_OPENSSL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ZLIB
	help
	  The user-space half of the Linux support for the Focusrite
	  interfaces that speak the Focusrite Control Protocol: the
	  Scarlett 16i16, 18i16 and 18i20 of the fourth generation and
	  the ISA C8X. The kernel driver (sound/usb/fcp.c, in Linux
	  since 6.14) only carries messages to and from the interface;
	  what they mean is known here.

	  fcp-server, started by udev for each such interface, reads
	  its router, mixer and preamplifier settings and shows them as
	  ALSA controls, the ones dawos-card-setup reads and writes.
	  Without it the interface plays and records, with whatever
	  routing it has in its memory, and nothing can be read or
	  changed.

	  fcp-tool lists the interfaces with the version of their
	  firmware and updates it, from the files of the package
	  scarlett4-firmware.

	  https://github.com/geoffreybennett/fcp-support
